reading-time plugin: {
  textOnPage: 'As generative AI evolves, the tools used to orchestrate these models must also advance. Gemini 3 provides developers with a powerful new model, but raw API calls rarely suffice for production environments. To build robust applications, you need a framework that manages state, streaming, structured data, and external APIs.This post explores how to integrate Gemini 3 with LangChain, bridge the frontend-backend gap using LangServe, and build model-agnostic applications that work across OpenAI and Anthropic.Gemini 3 and LangChainLangChain supports Gemini 3 through the @langchain/google-genai package. Because Gemini 3 maintains compatibility with existing API infrastructure, you can often upgrade your application by simply updating the model string.PrerequisitesInstall the necessary packages:npm install @langchain/google-genai @langchain/core zodBasic Setup and StreamingLatency significantly impacts user experience. In modern AI applications, you should stream responses so users do not have to wait for a full block of text. LangChain’s .stream() method handles this logic and helps future-proof your application against longer model response times.import { ChatGoogleGenerativeAI } from "@langchain/google-genai";\n' +
    '\n' +
    'async function runGeminiStream() {\n' +
    '  const model = new ChatGoogleGenerativeAI({\n' +
    '    model: "gemini-3.0-pro",\n' +
    '    apiKey: process.env.GOOGLE_API_KEY,\n' +
    '  });\n' +
    '\n' +
    '  console.log("--- Starting Stream ---");\n' +
    '\n' +
    '  const stream = await model.stream("Explain quantum computing in one sentence.");\n' +
    '\n' +
    '  for await (const chunk of stream) {\n' +
    '    process.stdout.write(chunk.content as string);\n' +
    '  }\n' +
    '}\n' +
    '\n' +
    'runGeminiStream().catch(console.error);Structured Output with ZodExtracting usable JSON from a Large Language Model (LLM) is a common challenge. While you can prompt Gemini for “JSON only,” the results are often fragile. Using withStructuredOutput combined with Zod ensures type safety and runtime validation.import { ChatGoogleGenerativeAI } from "@langchain/google-genai";\n' +
    'import { z } from "zod";\n' +
    '\n' +
    'const recipeSchema = z.object({\n' +
    '  name: z.string().describe("The name of the dish"),\n' +
    '  ingredients: z.array(z.string()).describe("List of ingredients"),\n' +
    '  prepTime: z.number().describe("Preparation time in minutes"),\n' +
    '  difficulty: z.enum(["Easy", "Medium", "Hard"]),\n' +
    '});\n' +
    '\n' +
    'type Recipe = z.infer<typeof recipeSchema>;\n' +
    '\n' +
    'async function generateRecipe() {\n' +
    '  const model = new ChatGoogleGenerativeAI({\n' +
    '    model: "gemini-3.0-pro",\n' +
    '    temperature: 0,\n' +
    '    apiKey: process.env.GOOGLE_API_KEY,\n' +
    '  });\n' +
    '\n' +
    '  const structuredLlm = model.withStructuredOutput(recipeSchema);\n' +
    '  const result = await structuredLlm.invoke("How do I make scrambled eggs?");\n' +
    '\n' +
    '  console.log(`Cooking ${result.name} will take ${result.prepTime} minutes.`);\n' +
    '}The LangServe ArchitectureMany enterprise stacks pair a fast TypeScript frontend with a Python-based data science ecosystem on the backend. LangServe wraps your Python LangChain code and deploys it as a REST API, which removes the need for manual FastAPI boilerplate.Step 1: The Python ServerThis script runs on your backend and exposes your application logic.import uvicorn\n' +
    'from fastapi import FastAPI\n' +
    'from langchain_openai import ChatOpenAI\n' +
    'from langchain_core.prompts import ChatPromptTemplate\n' +
    'from langserve import add_routes\n' +
    '\n' +
    '# 1. Define the Chain\n' +
    'model = ChatOpenAI(model="gpt-4o")\n' +
    'prompt = ChatPromptTemplate.from_template("Explain {topic} to a 5-year-old.")\n' +
    'chain = prompt | model\n' +
    '\n' +
    '# 2. Initialize FastAPI\n' +
    'app = FastAPI(\n' +
    '  title="AI Logic Server",\n' +
    '  version="1.0",\n' +
    `  description="An API server using LangChain's Runnable interfaces",\n` +
    ')\n' +
    '\n' +
    '# 3. Add Routes\n' +
    '# This creates /explain/invoke and /explain/stream endpoints automatically\n' +
    'add_routes(\n' +
    '  app,\n' +
    '  chain,\n' +
    '  path="/explain",\n' +
    ')\n' +
    '\n' +
    'if __name__ == "__main__":\n' +
    '  uvicorn.run(app, host="localhost", port=8000)Step 2: The TypeScript ClientFrom your frontend, the remote server behaves exactly like a local function.import { RemoteRunnable } from "@langchain/core/runnables/remote";\n' +
    '\n' +
    'async function runRemoteChain() {\n' +
    '  const remoteChain = new RemoteRunnable({\n' +
    '    url: "http://localhost:8000/explain",\n' +
    '  });\n' +
    '\n' +
    '  const result = (await remoteChain.invoke({\n' +
    '    topic: "Black Holes",\n' +
    '  })) as { content: string };\n' +
    '\n' +
    '  console.log("Response from Python:", result.content);\n' +
    '}Working with External APIsReal-world applications must fetch and process external data. LangChain provides two patterns for this: a Query Builder for inputs and RunnableLambda for outputs.Composing Fetch Queries (The Query Builder)Avoid asking an LLM to generate a raw URL, as this often leads to syntax errors. Instead, request structured parameters from the LLM and use your code to construct the URL safely.import { ChatGoogleGenerativeAI } from "@langchain/google-genai";\n' +
    'import { z } from "zod";\n' +
    '\n' +
    'const searchParamsSchema = z.object({\n' +
    '  query: z.string(),\n' +
    '  status: z.enum(["active", "archived"]).optional(),\n' +
    '  limit: z.number().min(1).max(50).default(10),\n' +
    '  sortBy: z.enum(["date", "relevance"]).default("date"),\n' +
    '});\n' +
    '\n' +
    'async function composeQuery() {\n' +
    '  const model = new ChatGoogleGenerativeAI({ model: "gemini-3.0-pro" });\n' +
    '  const queryGenerator = model.withStructuredOutput(searchParamsSchema);\n' +
    '\n' +
    '  const params = await queryGenerator.invoke(\n' +
    '    "Find me the last 5 active user logs sorted by date."\n' +
    '  );\n' +
    '\n' +
    '  const queryString = new URLSearchParams({\n' +
    '    q: params.query,\n' +
    '    limit: params.limit.toString(),\n' +
    '    sort: params.sortBy,\n' +
    '    ...(params.status && { status: params.status }),\n' +
    '  }).toString();\n' +
    '\n' +
    '  console.log(`URL: /api/logs?${queryString}`);\n' +
    '}Processing API Results (The Runnable Pattern)Wrap your fetch logic in a RunnableLambda to inject external data directly into a LangChain pipeline.import { RunnableSequence, RunnableLambda } from "@langchain/core/runnables";\n' +
    '\n' +
    'const apiStep = new RunnableLambda({\n' +
    '  func: async (input: { id: string }) => {\n' +
    '    // Standard fetch logic\n' +
    '    return { id: input.id, uptime: 99.9, logs: ["Critical Error"] };\n' +
    '  },\n' +
    '});\n' +
    '\n' +
    'const chain = RunnableSequence.from([\n' +
    '  { api_data: apiStep },\n' +
    '  prompt,\n' +
    '  model,\n' +
    ']);\n' +
    '\n' +
    'await chain.invoke({ id: "server-01" });Multi-Model SupportA factory function allows you to switch the “brain” of your application without altering your core business logic.import { ChatGoogleGenerativeAI } from "@langchain/google-genai";\n' +
    'import { ChatOpenAI } from "@langchain/openai";\n' +
    'import { ChatAnthropic } from "@langchain/anthropic";\n' +
    'import { BaseChatModel } from "@langchain/core/language_models/chat_models";\n' +
    '\n' +
    'function getModel(provider: "google" | "openai" | "anthropic"): BaseChatModel {\n' +
    '  const config = { apiKey: process.env.API_KEY };\n' +
    '\n' +
    '  switch (provider) {\n' +
    '    case "google":\n' +
    '      return new ChatGoogleGenerativeAI({ model: "gemini-3.0-pro", ...config });\n' +
    '    case "openai":\n' +
    '      return new ChatOpenAI({ model: "gpt-4o", ...config });\n' +
    '    case "anthropic":\n' +
    '      return new ChatAnthropic({ model: "claude-3-5-sonnet-latest", ...config });\n' +
    '    default:\n' +
    '      throw new Error("Unknown provider");\n' +
    '  }\n' +
    '}\n' +
    '\n' +
    'async function main() {\n' +
    '  const model = getModel("openai");\n' +
    '  const response = await model.invoke("What is the capital of France?");\n' +
    '  console.log(response.content);\n' +
    '}\n' +
    'main().catch(console.error);SummaryGemini 3 integrates seamlessly using the gemini-3.0-pro model string.Structured Output with Zod is the industry standard for reliable data parsing.LangServe connects Python-heavy AI logic to TypeScript frontends efficiently.External APIs remain secure when you use the Query Builder pattern for parameter management.Multi-Provider Support allows you to switch models by instantiating different classes.',
  readingTime: { text: '5 min read', minutes: 4.4, time: 264000, words: 880 }
}
