    '`<footer>` for landmarks.\n' +
    '- Use `<h1>`-`<h6>` in correct hierarchical order. Do\n' +
    'not skip levels.\n' +
    '- Use `<ul>`/`<ol>` with `<li>` for lists.\n' +
    '- Use `<table>`, `<thead>`, `<tbody>`, `<th>`, `<td>` for tabular data.\n' +
    '- Use `<form>`, `<fieldset>`, `<legend>`,\n' +
    '`<label>` for forms.\n' +
    '- Use `<dialog>` for modal dialogs with its showModal() API.\n' +
    '- Use `<details>`/`<summary>` for simple disclosures when appropriate.\n' +
    '\n' +
    '## Accessibility\n' +
    '- Every interactive element must have an accessible name\n' +
    '  (visible text, aria-label, or aria-labelledby).\n' +
    '- Every form input must have an associated `<label>` or\n' +
    '  `aria-label`.\n' +
    '- Icon-only buttons: `aria-label` on button,\n' +
    '\t`aria-hidden` on icon.\n' +
    '- Decorative images: `alt=""` or `aria-hidden="true"`.\n' +
    '- Dynamic state: use `aria-expanded`, `aria-selected`,\n' +
