reading-time plugin: {
  textOnPage: 'Building a ServiceWorker using Google librariesGoogle provides an abstraction layer over Service Workers called sw-toolbox that hides a lot of the complexities of a Service Worker without sacrificing functionality.The example below uses sw-toolbox to create a serviceworker that precaches the application shell and treats everything else as a default with a network-first&nbsp; strategy.(global => {\n' +
    "  'use strict';\n" +
    '\n' +
    '  // Load the sw-toolbox library.\n' +
    "  importScripts('bower_components/sw-toolbox/sw-toolbox.js');\n" +
    '\n' +
    '  // List of files to precache. This should be automated.\n' +
    '  const FILES_TO_PRECACHE = [\n' +
    "    'index.html',\n" +
    "    'js/app.js',\n" +
    "    'css/main.css',\n" +
    "    '/images/logo.svg',\n" +
    "    'offline.html'\n" +
    '  ];\n' +
    '\n' +
    "  // Turn on debug logging, visible in the Developer Tools' console.\n" +
    '  global.toolbox.options.debug = true;\n' +
    '\n' +
    '  // precache the files in FILES_TO_PRECACHE\n' +
    '  global.toolbox.precache(FILES_TO_PRECACHE);\n' +
    '\n' +
    '  // By default, all requests will use the toolbox.networkFirst cache\n' +
    '  // strategy, and their responses will be stored in the default cache.\n' +
    '  global.toolbox.router.default = global.toolbox.networkFirst;\n' +
    '\n' +
    '  // Boilerplate to ensure our service worker takes control of the page \n' +
    '  // as soon as possible.\n' +
    "  global.addEventListener('install',\n" +
    '      event => event.waitUntil(global.skipWaiting()));\n' +
    "  global.addEventListener('activate',\n" +
    '      event => event.waitUntil(global.clients.claim()));\n' +
    '})(self);Building a ServiceWorker using Polymer Platinum ElementsThis is not an article about Polymer or the platinum-sw element. It is mentioned just for completeness sake.Polymer provides elements to create Service Workers and cache sitting on top of sw-toolbox. The partial example below, taken from the platinum-sw distribution shows how to configure the Polymer Service Worker element .We can also choose to incorporate the platinum-sw element inside other elements like we do for our Ajax calls.    <template is="dom-bind" id="page-template">\n' +
    '      <platinum -sw-register skip-waiting\n' +
    '                            clients-claim\n' +
    '                            reload-on-install\n' +
    '                            state="{{state}}">\n' +
    '        </platinum><platinum -sw-cache default-cache-strategy="networkFirst"\n' +
    '                           precache="{{precacheList}}"></platinum>The precacheList element can be created manually or automated as part of a build process.',
  readingTime: { text: '2 min read', minutes: 1.275, time: 76500, words: 255 }
}
