reading-time plugin: {
  textOnPage: 'Ever since I wrote my original research on paged media the specs have changed considerably. Here’s an update based on the following specifications:CSS Paged Media Level 3 Working Draft from 3/14/13CSS Generated Content for Paged Media Module editor draft from 8/7/14Antenna House Formatter Online Manual downloaded 8/17/14Prince XML User Guide last accessed 8/17/14I’ve also tailored the project to work with Antenna House Formatter and Prince XML. Some of the idiosyncracies will come up while developing the stylesheet for this project.HTML to be used in these examplesThe basic HTML file that will be used throughout these examples is below. It’s not a complete example by any stretch of the imagination but it will be enough to get us started.<html>\n' +
    '<head>\n' +
    '<title>My Awesome Book</title>\n' +
    '<meta charset="utf-8">\n' +
    '</head>\n' +
    "<body data-type='book'>\n" +
    "<section data-type='titlepage'>\n" +
    "<h1 class='title'>Lorem Ipsum</h1>\n" +
    "<h2 class='author'>Carlos Araya</h2>\n" +
    '</section>\n' +
    '<section data-type="toc">\n' +
    '  <!-- TO BE POPULATED LATER-->\n' +
    '</section>\n' +
    "<section data-type='chapter'>\n" +
    '  <p class="rh">Introduction</p>\n' +
    '  <h1>Introduction</h1>\n' +
    '  <p>Lórem ípsum dolór sít amet, vix graeco minímum no. Iudicó atomorum praesent cum éi. Méa quem accumsan adversárium ño, ut mea illum corpora. Vídit aperiri partieñdo iñ duo, vel dicta antiopam médiocrem ád. Et omnés dolorúm perpetua eúm, est át ália labore adversaríum.\n' +
    '  </p>\n' +
    '  <p>\n' +
    ' Usu et adhuc phaedrum philosophiá, nec posidónium mediocritatem et, dólorum euripidis mediocritátem per et. Vís harum adipiscing ei. Et eos qúañdo primis quodsi. Nullám accusata expetenda mel et. Facilisi deseruísse qui at, módo tritáñi legéndos id ius. Denique splendide dispútando ad sit, néc ex tale bonorum consulatu.\n' +
    '  </p>\n' +
    '  </section>\n' +
    '  </body>\n' +
    '  </html>There are a few things to notice:This is not a complete document. It lacks many of the features from the stylesheetEach chapter title is set up twiceFirst as a paragraph with rh class that we’ll take out of the regular flow of text and use as our running headerThe second one, wrapped on h1 tags, will be shown as part of the flow of textInstead of classes or ID attributes, we use data-type attributes to model after epub and the epub:type attributesDefining the base pageTo define the base page we’ve used the following three elementsThe first one defines our default page and attributes. We reset the counter for every page and lay the footnotes at the bottom of every page spanning all potential columns and allowing the height to take as much as it needs to in order to fill the content.@page {\n' +
    '  size: 8.5in 11in;\n' +
    '  margin: 0.5in 1in;\n' +
    '  /* Footnote related attributes */\n' +
    '  counter-reset: footnote;\n' +
    '  @footnote {\n' +
    '    counter-increment: footnote;\n' +
    '    float: bottom;\n' +
    '    column-span: all;\n' +
    '    height: auto;\n' +
    '    }\n' +
    '  }For the chapter page we set up the layout of a running footer but doesn’t tell the page what the content of the footer is, just placement and content@page chapter {\n' +
    '  @bottom-center {\n' +
    '    vertical-align: middle;\n' +
    '    content: element(heading);\n' +
    '  }\n' +
    '}For the body of our CSS, body tag where the data-type is book, we set up a CMYK color rather than RGB as CMYK is what printers use. We also setup automatic hyphenation for the entire document so we don’t have to worry about it later.body[data-type="book"] {\n' +
    '  color: cmyk(0%,0%,100%,100%);\n' +
    '  hyphns: auto;\n' +
    '}Counters/* page counters  */\n' +
    'body[data-type="book"] > div[data-type="part"]:first-of-type,\n' +
    'body[data-type="book"] > section[data-type="chapter"]:first-of-type { counter-reset: page 1 }\n' +
    'body[data-type="book"] > section[data-type="chapter"]+div[data-type="part"] { counter-reset: none }We are setting page counters up so that they’ll reset when we want them to. We set the following scenarios:When there is a part element that is the first of type direct child of book body[data-type="book"] > div[data-type="part"]:first-of-type orThere is a chapter child that is the first of type direct descendant of book body[data-type="book"] > div[data-type="part"]:first-of-typeThen reset the counters for page to 1.if the first direct child of a book is a chapter that has a part siblibling body[data-type="book"] > section[data-type="chapter"]+div[data-type="part"] { counter-reset: none }Do not reset the page counterTitle Page/* Title Page*/\n' +
    'section[data-type="titlepage"] { page: titlepage }\n' +
    'section[data-type="titlepage"] * { text-align: center }\n' +
    'For the title page we made minimal customizations, we could definitely do more. We have chosen to align all the contentFront MatterWe define a series of pages to handle our front matter. We could define fewer pages but then we’d have to create them as we need them and that’s work we don’t need to do unless we really need toCopyright/* Copyright page */\n' +
    'section[data-type="copyright"] { page: copyright }We define a page for copyright and other legal information. We are leaving it empty by default.Dedication/* Dedication */\n' +
    'section[data-type="dedication"] { page: dedication }\n' +
    'section[data-type="dedication"] p { font-style: italic }\n' +
    'section[data-type="dedication"] * { text-align: center }For the dedication element we center all the content and we make all paragraphs italic.Table of Content/* TOC */\n' +
    'nav[data-type="toc"] { page: toc }\n' +
    'nav[data-type="toc"] ol { list-style-type: none }Make the nav containing our TOC have an ordered list without numbers. This is the best semantics for the TOC I’ve found.Foreword and Preface/* Foreword  */\n' +
    'section[data-type="foreword"] { page: foreword }\n' +
    '\n' +
    '/* Preface*/\n' +
    'section[data-type="preface"] { page: preface }We mark both of these sections up but we don’t do any particular styling for them, not yetFront Matter Page Definition/* Comon Front Mater Page Numbering in lowercase ROMAN numerals*/\n' +
    '/* Right Side */\n' +
    '@page toc:right {\n' +
    '  @bottom-right-corner { content: counter(page, lower-roman) }\n' +
    '  @bottom-left-corner { content: normal }\n' +
    '}\n' +
    '\n' +
    '@page foreword:right {\n' +
    '  @bottom-right-corner { content: counter(page, lower-roman) }\n' +
    '  @bottom-left-corner { content: normal }\n' +
    '}\n' +
    '\n' +
    '@page preface:right {\n' +
    '  @bottom-right-corner { content: counter(page, lower-roman) }\n' +
    '  @bottom-left-corner { content: normal }\n' +
    '}\n' +
    '\n' +
    '/* Left Side*/\n' +
    '@page toc:left  {\n' +
    '  @bottom-left-corner { content: counter(page, lower-roman) }\n' +
    '  @bottom-right-corner { content: normal }\n' +
    '}\n' +
    '\n' +
    '@page foreword:left  {\n' +
    '  @bottom-left-corner { content: counter(page, lower-roman) }\n' +
    '  @bottom-right-corner { content: normal }\n' +
    '}\n' +
    '\n' +
    '@page preface:left  {\n' +
    '  @bottom-left-corner { content: counter(page, lower-roman) }\n' +
    '  @bottom-right-corner { content: normal }\n' +
    '}We define each set of pages (left and right) to allow setup of different elements on each facing page. On the left side pages, we place the page number on the bottom left corner and we set it in the opposite corner on the right side. The page number is in addition to the running footer we set earlierParts, Chapters and Appendices/* Part */\n' +
    'div[data-type="part"] { page: part }Parts are the largest containers for our books, Right now they have no other definition but can be further extended/* Chapter */\n' +
    'section[data-type="chapter"] {\n' +
    '  page: chapter;\n' +
    '  page-break-before: always;\n' +
    '}\n' +
    '\n' +
    '/* Appendix */\n' +
    'section[data-type="appendix"] {\n' +
    '  page: appendix;\n' +
    '  page-break-before: always;\n' +
    '}Chapters and Appendices always start at the top of a page by using the page-break-before selector set to always.Back Matter/* Glossary */\n' +
    'section[data-type="glossary"] { page: glossary }\n' +
    '\n' +
    '/* Bibliography */\n' +
    'section[data-type="bibliography"] { page: bibliography }\n' +
    '\n' +
    '/* Index */\n' +
    'section[data-type="index"] { page: index }\n' +
    '\n' +
    '/* Colophon */\n' +
    'section[data-type="colophon"] { page: colophon }The glossary, bibliography, index and colophon (to which I refer to as back matter) are set up with their own pages which we can style later.Content Sections and Page Numbering/* Common Content Page Numbering  in Arabic numerals 1... 199 */\n' +
    '@page titlepage{ /* Need this to clean up page numbers in titlepage in Prince*/\n' +
    '  @bottom-right-corner { content: normal }\n' +
    '  @bottom-left-corner { content: normal }\n' +
    '}\n' +
    '\n' +
    '/* Right Side*/\n' +
    '@page chapter:right  {\n' +
    '  @bottom-right-corner { content: counter(page) }\n' +
    '  @bottom-left-corner { content: normal }\n' +
    '}\n' +
    '\n' +
    '@page appendix:right  {\n' +
    '  @bottom-right-corner { content: counter(page) }\n' +
    '  @bottom-left-corner { content: normal }\n' +
    '}\n' +
    '\n' +
    '@page glossary:right,  {\n' +
    '  @bottom-right-corner { content: counter(page) }\n' +
    '  @bottom-left-corner { content: normal }\n' +
    '}\n' +
    '\n' +
    '@page bibliography:right  {\n' +
    '  @bottom-right-corner { content: counter(page) }\n' +
    '  @bottom-left-corner { content: normal }\n' +
    '}\n' +
    '\n' +
    '@page index:right  {\n' +
    '  @bottom-right-corner { content: counter(page) }\n' +
    '  @bottom-left-corner { content: normal }\n' +
    '}\n' +
    '\n' +
    '/* Left Side */\n' +
    '@page chapter:left {\n' +
    '  @bottom-left-corner { content: counter(page) }\n' +
    '  @bottom-right-corner { content: normal }\n' +
    '}\n' +
    '\n' +
    '@page appendix:left {\n' +
    '  @bottom-left-corner { content: counter(page) }\n' +
    '  @bottom-right-corner { content: normal }\n' +
    '}\n' +
    '\n' +
    '@page glossary:left, {\n' +
    '  @bottom-left-corner { content: counter(page) }\n' +
    '  @bottom-right-corner { content: normal }\n' +
    '}\n' +
    '\n' +
    '@page bibliography:left {\n' +
    '  @bottom-left-corner { content: counter(page) }\n' +
    '  @bottom-right-corner { content: normal }\n' +
    '}\n' +
    '\n' +
