reading-time plugin: {
  textOnPage: 'Standard YouTube embeds are notoriously heavy. A single <iframe> can download over 1MB of JavaScript and block the main thread, significantly hurting the Largest Contentful Paint (LCP). Furthermore, if dimensions are not strictly reserved, the embed causes Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS) as it loads.This post documents the process of building a production-grade embed component that solves these issues using Web Components and React.The core problemsDevelopers must address three primary issues with the standard YouTube embed:Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS)When an iframe loads, it often starts with zero height and then “pops” open to its full size, pushing content down.Legacy solution: The “Padding Hack” (using padding-bottom: 56.25% on a wrapper).Modern solution: The CSS aspect-ratio property.Page weight (LCP and TBT)Loading the YouTube player API immediately—even if the user never plays the video—wastes bandwidth and CPU resources.Solution: The Facade Pattern. The application loads a lightweight static image (the video thumbnail) and a fake play button. The heavy iframe is only injected into the DOM when the user clicks.Audio chaosIf a user plays one video, then scrolls down and plays another, both audio streams will play simultaneously.Solution: Singleton State. When a component activates, it broadcasts a message to all other components to pause or reset their state.The strategy: “Lite mode” (facade pattern)Instead of rendering an <iframe> immediately, the component renders this lightweight HTML structure:HTML<div class="container">\n' +
    '  <!-- 15KB image instead of 1MB of JavaScript -->\n' +
    '  <img\n' +
    '    src="https://i.ytimg.com/vi/{ID}/hqdefault.jpg"\n' +
    '    loading="lazy"\n' +
    '    alt="Video Thumbnail">\n' +
    '  <button class="play-btn" aria-label="Play Video"></button>\n' +
    '</div>On click, the component replaces the inner HTML with the iframe, appending ?autoplay=1 to the source URL so the video starts immediately.Handling dimensions and aspect ratioThis implementation uses a priority system to handle both responsive and fixed layouts without introducing layout shifts. Based on the HTML attributes or React props provided, the component calculates and applies specific CSS properties (width, height, and aspect-ratio) to its outer container.ScenarioAttributes ProvidedWidthHeightAspect RatioResponsiveNone (default)100%auto16 / 9Fixedwidth=“500” height=“300”500px300pxautoCustom Ratioaspect-ratio=“4/3”100%auto4 / 3Logic flowflowchart TD\n' +
    '    Start([Start]) --> CheckFixed{Width & Height<br/>Both Set?}\n' +
    '\n' +
    '    CheckFixed -- Yes --> FixedMode[Fixed Mode]\n' +
    '    FixedMode --> ApplyFixed["Set width = attr<br/>Set height = attr<br/>Set aspect-ratio = auto"]\n' +
    '\n' +
    '    CheckFixed -- No --> CheckWidth{Width Set?}\n' +
    '\n' +
    '    CheckWidth -- Yes --> WidthMode[Width-Only Mode]\n' +
    '    WidthMode --> ApplyWidth["Set width = attr<br/>Set height = auto<br/>Set aspect-ratio = auto"]\n' +
    '\n' +
    '    CheckWidth -- No --> ResponsiveMode[Responsive Mode]\n' +
    '    ResponsiveMode --> SetDefaults["Set width = 100%<br/>Set height = auto"]\n' +
    '    SetDefaults --> CheckRatio{Aspect Ratio<br/>Set?}\n' +
    '\n' +
    '    CheckRatio -- Yes --> ApplyCustomRatio[Set aspect-ratio = attr]\n' +
    '    CheckRatio -- No --> ApplyDefaultRatio[Set aspect-ratio = 16/9]Logic descriptionIf width and height exist: Force fixed dimensions; set aspect-ratio: auto.If only width exists: Set width; reset height to auto.Default: Set width to 100%; use the provided aspect-ratio (defaults to 16/9).The singleton pattern (audio management)To prevent multiple videos from playing at once, the architecture utilizes the global window event bus.Listen: Every component listens for a custom event (youtube-embed-activate).Dispatch: When a user clicks a video, that specific component dispatches the event with its own unique ID.React: If a component receives the event and the ID does not match its own, it resets its state to active: false (removing the iframe and displaying the thumbnail again).Event bus visualizationsequenceDiagram\n' +
    '    participant User\n' +
    '    participant CompA as Component A (Clicked)\n' +
    '    participant Window as Window (Event Bus)\n' +
    '    participant CompB as Component B (Playing)\n' +
    '\n' +
    '    User->>CompA: Clicks Play\n' +
    '    CompA->>CompA: Set State = Active\n' +
    "    CompA->>Window: Dispatch 'youtube-embed-activate' {id: A}\n" +
    '\n' +
    '    par Broadcast Event\n' +
    '        Window->>CompB: Event {id: A}\n' +
    '        CompB->>CompB: Check ID (A != B)\n' +
    '        CompB->>CompB: Set State = Inactive (Reset to Thumbnail)\n' +
    '    and\n' +
    '        Window->>CompA: Event {id: A}\n' +
    '        CompA->>CompA: Check ID (A == A)\n' +
    '        CompA->>CompA: Ignore (Remain Active)\n' +
    '    endWeb Component implementationDevelopers can drop this standalone component into any project (Vanilla JavaScript, Vue, Angular, Svelte) to use the <youtube-embed> tag natively.TypeScriptclass YouTubeEmbed extends HTMLElement {\n' +
    "  private videoId = '';\n" +
    '  private boundResetHandler: (e: Event) => void;\n' +
    '\n' +
    '  constructor() {\n' +
    '    super();\n' +
    "    this.attachShadow({ mode: 'open' });\n" +
    '    this.boundResetHandler = this.handleExternalActivation.bind(this);\n' +
    '  }\n' +
    '\n' +
    '  connectedCallback(): void {\n' +
    "    this.videoId = this.getAttribute('video-id') || '';\n" +
    '    if (!this.videoId) return;\n' +
    '\n' +
    '    // Dimension Logic\n' +
    "    const widthAttr = this.getAttribute('width');\n" +
    "    const heightAttr = this.getAttribute('height');\n" +
    "    const ratioAttr = this.getAttribute('aspect-ratio');\n" +
    '\n' +
    "    let width = '100%';\n" +
    "    let height = 'auto';\n" +
    "    let ratio = '16 / 9';\n" +
    '\n' +
    '    if (widthAttr && heightAttr) {\n' +
    '      width = this.formatDim(widthAttr);\n' +
    '      height = this.formatDim(heightAttr);\n' +
    "      ratio = 'auto';\n" +
    '    } else if (widthAttr && !heightAttr) {\n' +
    '      width = this.formatDim(widthAttr);\n' +
    "      height = 'auto';\n" +
    "      ratio = 'auto';\n" +
    '    } else {\n' +
    '      if (ratioAttr) ratio = ratioAttr;\n' +
    '      if (widthAttr) width = this.formatDim(widthAttr);\n' +
