reading-time plugin: {
  textOnPage: 'Reactivity seems to be an important concept to learn as you work in front-end development.The idea is that your app’s UI will reflect changes as soon as they happen without requiring a full page reload.In this post, we’ll look at What is reactivity, how it works using three different approaches, and an example of using reactivity in front-end projectsWhat is reactivityIn the context of front-end development, reactivity programming deals with data streams and the propagation of change.In reactive programming, data is modeled as a sequence of events, and the application reacts to these events by updating its state.Understanding Typescript proxiesUnderstanding observablesUnderstanding the pub/sub patternLinks and ResourcesProxy Global ObjectHow vanilla JS Proxies workReactive Data With Modern JavaScriptThe Magic Behind Reactivity – ProxiesBuild Your Own Reactive System like Vue.jsLooking at All 13 JavaScript Proxy TrapsBuild Reactive UI with Plain JavascriptObserver and PubSub PatternHow to Build Your Own Reactivity SystemReactive UI’s with VanillaJS – Part 1: Pure Functional StyleReactive Programming in Vanilla JavascriptBuilding stateful web apps without ReactSimplifying Front-End State Management with Observable StoreA high way to ObservablesTools and librariesvan.jsCausalityRx.jsKefir.js<!--\n' +
    '<https://gomakethings.com/how-to-create-a-state-based-ui-component-with-vanilla-js/>\n' +
    '\n' +
    '<https://gomakethings.com/simple-reactive-data-stores-with-vanilla-javascript-and-proxies/>\n' +
    '\n' +
    '<https://gomakethings.com/how-to-detect-changes-to-nested-arrays-and-objects-inside-a-proxy/>\n' +
    '\n' +
    '<https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nREQw5uKhkw>\n' +
    '--><!--\n' +
    '## Understanding how to add reactivity with Vanilla Javascript\n' +
    '\n' +
    '```js\n' +
    "function store (data = {}, name = 'store') {\n" +
    '\n' +
    '  /**\n' +
    '   * Emit a custom event\n' +
    '   * @param  {String} type   The event type\n' +
    '   * @param  {*}      detail Any details to pass along with the event\n' +
    '   */\n' +
    '  function emit (type, detail) {\n' +
    '\n' +
    '    // Create a new event\n' +
    '    let event = new CustomEvent(type, {\n' +
    '      bubbles: true,\n' +
    '      cancelable: true,\n' +
    '      detail: detail\n' +
    '    });\n' +
    '\n' +
    '    // Dispatch the event\n' +
    '    return document.dispatchEvent(event);\n' +
    '\n' +
    '  }\n' +
    '\n' +
    '  function handler (name, data) {\n' +
    '    return {\n' +
    '      get: function (obj, prop) {\n' +
    "        if (prop === '_isProxy') return true;\n" +
    "        if (['object', 'array'].includes(Object.prototype.toString.call(obj[prop]).slice(8, -1).toLowerCase()) && !obj[prop]._isProxy) {\n" +
    '          obj[prop] = new Proxy(obj[prop], handler(name, data));\n' +
    '        }\n' +
    '        return obj[prop];\n' +
    '      },\n' +
    '      set: function (obj, prop, value) {\n' +
    '        if (obj[prop] === value) return true;\n' +
    '        obj[prop] = value;\n' +
    '        emit(name, data);\n' +
    '        return true;\n' +
    '      },\n' +
    '      deleteProperty: function (obj, prop) {\n' +
    '        delete obj[prop];\n' +
    '        emit(name, data);\n' +
    '        return true;\n' +
    '      }\n' +
    '    };\n' +
    '  }\n' +
    '\n' +
    '  return new Proxy(data, handler(name, data));\n' +
    '\n' +
    '}\n' +
    '\n' +
    '// The element to inject our UI into\n' +
    "let app = document.querySelector('#app');\n" +
    '\n' +
    '// Create reactive data store\n' +
    "let wizards = store(['Gandalf', 'Merlin'], 'wizards');\n" +
    '\n' +
    '// The template\n' +
    'function template (props) {\n' +
    '  return `\n' +
    '    <ul>\n' +
    '      ${props.map(function (wizard) {\n' +
    '        return `<li>${wizard}</li>`;\n' +
    "      }).join('')}\n" +
    '    </ul>`;\n' +
    '}\n' +
    '\n' +
    '// Render the UI\n' +
    'app.innerHTML = template(wizards);\n' +
    '\n' +
    '// Reactively update the UI\n' +
    "document.addEventListener('wizards', function (event) {\n" +
    '  app.innerHTML = template(event.detail);\n' +
    '});\n' +
    '\n' +
    '// This will automatically update the UI\n' +
    'setTimeout(function () {\n' +
    "  wizards.push('Ursula');\n" +
    '}, 3000);\n' +
    '```\n' +
    '-->',
  readingTime: { text: '3 min read', minutes: 2.04, time: 122400, words: 408 }
}
