reading-time plugin: {
  textOnPage: "In The File System Access API: simplifying access to local files, the authors describe how to use the API to create file management functionality for web applicationsThe idea is that we’ll be able to open a file from, display it in the browser and then if desired, save it to a new location in our local file system.To open a file we’ll use the following code.We define the following constants and variables:Capture the button to open a fileCapture the button to save a fileCapture the text area where we’ll insert the textCapture the content that we’ll saveSets up an empty variable for the filehandle we want to work withconst openButton = document.querySelector('.openButton');\n" +
    "const saveButton = document.querySelector('.saveButton');\n" +
    "const display = document.querySelector('.content-area');\n" +
    'const dataToSave = display.innerText;\n' +
    'let fileHandle;The openFile function is called when the open file button is clicked. It opens the file, reads the content, and puts the content in the text area.The function runs the following steps:We use feature detection to make sure the feature is supported, if not then we bailWe create a new filehandle and show the file picker dialogueOpen the fileRead and convert the content of the file to textInsert the content of the file into the display text area{.custom-ordered}async function openFile() {\n' +
    "  if ('showOpenFilePicker' in window) { // 1\n" +
    '    [fileHandle] = await window.showOpenFilePicker(); // 2\n' +
    '    const file = await fileHandle.getFile(); // 3\n' +
    '    const contents = await file.text(); // 4\n' +
    '    display.innerText = contents; // 5\n' +
    '  } else {\n' +
    "    console.error('filehandle API not supported');\n" +
    '  }\n' +
    '}Saving a fileSaving a file is a little more complicated. We need to create a new filehandle, capture the content to save, write the content to the file and then close the file and save it.The steps are as follows:Use a feature query to detect if showSaveFilePicker is supported. If it’s not then bailShow the save file pickerCreate a FileSystemWritableFileStream to write toWrite the fileclose the file and write the contents to disk.{.custom-ordered}async function saveFile() {\n' +
    "  if ('showSaveFilePicker' in window) { // 1\n" +
    '    const newHandle = await window.showSaveFilePicker(); // 2\n' +
    '      const writableStream = await newHandle.createWritable(); // 3\n' +
    '        await writableStream.write(dataToSave); // 4\n' +
    '      await writableStream.close(); // 5\n' +
    '  }\n' +
    "}Finally, we attach the functions to the click event of the corresponding button.openButton.addEventListener('click', openFile);\n" +
    "saveButton.addEventListener('click', saveFile);Links and resourcesPublic explainerFile System Access and File specifications at WICGChromeStatus.com entryFile System Access API — MDNFile System Access API — Chromium Security Model",
  readingTime: { text: '2 min read', minutes: 1.955, time: 117300, words: 391 }
}
