reading-time plugin: {
  textOnPage: 'Now for what, to me, is the most tedious part of the workflow… copying things around and doing housekeeping on the files I’m working with.This is easier now since I don’t have to create directories (did that already) or move things around (only copy) so we set up tasks to copy sets of files and clean up after ourselves.Copying things overCopying files ended up being stranger than I thought it would be. I could set up a big task that would copy everything every time I run it but I realized that such a task would be overkill since some of the files do not update as often as others.So instead I created specific copy tasks. The first task will copy all content except the directories specified with a ! as the first character.There are no task specific plugins to install. It uses Gulp’s default API.// Copy all files at the root level (app)\n' +
    "gulp.task('copyAssets', function () {\n" +
    '  var APP_ASSETS = [\n' +
    "    'app/*',\n" +
    "    '!app/coffee',\n" +
    "    '!app/es6',\n" +
    "    '!app/scss',\n" +
    "    '!app/test',\n" +
    "    '!app/bower_components',\n" +
    "    '!app/fonts',\n" +
    "    '!app/cache-config.json',\n" +
    "    '!**/.DS_Store'\n" +
    '  ];\n' +
    '\n' +
    '  return gulp.src([ APP_ASSETS], {\n' +
    '    dot: true\n' +
    "  }).pipe(gulp.dest('dist'))\n" +
    '    .pipe($.size({\n' +
    '      pretty: true,\n' +
    "      title: 'copy'\n" +
    '    }));\n' +
    "});Copying content from the bower_components directory presents two options. If we’re working with a Polymer based application and we use Vulcanize to concatenate the components we use there are still components that cannot be included in the vulcanized output.gulp.task('copyBower', function () {\n" +
    '  var BOWER_ASSETS = [\n' +
    "    'bower_components/{webcomponentsjs,\n" +
    "platinum-sw,sw-toolbox,promise-polyfill}/**/*'\n" +
    '  ];\n' +
    '  return gulp.src([ BOWER_ASSETS], {\n' +
    '    dot: true\n' +
    "  }).pipe(gulp.dest('dist/elements'))\n" +
    '    .pipe($.size({\n' +
    '      pretty: true,\n' +
    "      title: 'copy'\n" +
    '    }));\n' +
    "});If we are not using Polymer you can still use Bower to install Javascript and CSS libraries. You can also save the dependencies to a bower.json and install them in a different system by using the command bower install.In this case we don’t specify the names of the plugins to copy. Instead we just do a blanket glob to copy everything under bower_componentsgulp.task('copyBower', function () {\n" +
    '  return gulp.src([\n' +
    "    'bower_components/**/*'\n" +
    '  ], {\n' +
    '    dot: true\n' +
    "  }).pipe(gulp.dest('dist'))\n" +
    '    .pipe($.size({\n' +
    '      pretty: true,\n' +
    "      title: 'copy'\n" +
    '    }));\n' +
    '});Web fonts change seldom, if at all. We copy everything inside the app/fonts directory over to the destination folder.// Copy web fonts to dist\n' +
    "gulp.task('copyFonts', function () {\n" +
    "  return gulp.src(['app/fonts/**'])\n" +
    "    .pipe(gulp.dest('dist'))\n" +
    '    .pipe($.size({\n' +
    "      title: 'fonts'\n" +
    '    }));\n' +
    '});Cleaning upI’m old enough to remember how leftovers would screw up compilation of a C program. To prevent that I usually create a task or a command to clean up the target directory from all existing crap. In this case the best way to do this is to remove a .tmp temporary directory and the dist directory that contains the results of all our tasks.Install the del plugin like this:npm install --save-dev  delThe task looks like this:// Clean output directory\n' +
    "gulp.task('clean', function () {\n" +
    ' return del.sync([\n' +
    "       'dist/',\n" +
    "   '.tmp'\n" +
    ' ]);\n' +
    '});',
  readingTime: { text: '3 min read', minutes: 2.26, time: 135600, words: 452 }
}
