reading-time plugin: {
  textOnPage: 'There are times when we need to add scripts to the page that will run only when there is a script already enqueued and loaded before it happens.I got bit by this when trying to use FontFaceObserver. For some reason, it worked fine in development but it would give a FontFaceObserver is not defined error when I moved the theme to production.The solution was hidden in some older documentation. As of version 4.5 there is an additional script loading function for loading inline scripts: wp_add_inline_script. This function allows adding inline scripts that depend on scriptsThe only important thing to remember is that this will only work when using a script that was enqueued using wp_enqueue_script.The final solution looks like this:function rivendellweb_enqueue_fontfaceobserver() {\n' +
    "  wp_enqueue_script( 'ffo_script',\n" +
    "    get_stylesheet_directory_uri() . '/js/fontfaceobserver.js',\n" +
    '    array(),\n' +
    "    '20151215',\n" +
    '    false );\n' +
    '\n' +
    `   wp_add_inline_script( 'ffo_script', 'const recursive = new FontFaceObserver("Recursive VF");let html = document.documentElement;\n` +
    '     Promise.all([recursive.load()]).then(() => {sessionStorage.fontsLoaded = true;console.log("Recursive has loaded.");\n' +
    '     }).catch((err) => {sessionStorage.fontsLoaded = false;console.log("Recursive failed to load", err);\n' +
    '     });\n' +
    '\n' +
    '     // Add a class based on whether the font loaded successfully\n' +
    '     if (sessionStorage.fontsLoaded) {html.classList.add("fonts-loaded");\n' +
    `     } else {html.classList.add("fonts-failed");}'\n` +
    '   );\n' +
    '}\n' +
    '\n' +
    "add_action( 'wp_enqueue_scripts', 'rivendellweb_enqueue_fontfaceobserver' );Links and ReferencesEnhanced Script Loader in WordPress 4.5Better Way to Add Inline Scriptswp_add_inline_script developer documentation",
  readingTime: { text: '1 min read', minutes: 0.98, time: 58800, words: 196 }
}
