reading-time plugin: {
  textOnPage: 'One of the biggest pains of working with Node is when either a library you’re working with is pinned to a specific version of Node or you must pin your project to a specific version because one or more dependencies will not work in versions after the specified one (or so the developers of the library say).This can happen in one of two ways.The supported versions are included in the engines section of the package.json file as an advisoryare included in a .nvmrc fileEven though neither of these options will stop you from running the package with an unsupported version, then it’s on you to fix any potential problems.The solutionOut of laziness, I use nvm, as my Node Version Manager.NVM helps me keep from having to manually install each version of Node that I want to keep around and makes sure that the packages of each version will not conflict with anotherWhen researching possible solutions, I came across this code, taken from this stack overflow answer.The idea is simple:If there is a .nvmrc file in the directory we change to then do the following:Run the specified versionIf the version is not installed, then install itIf the .nvmrc file is not present then the script will switch to the Node version indicated by the Node variable in NVM.The script will do the following:Capture local variablesCapture the current version of Node running in nvmCapture the path to the .nvmrc file if one existsIf there is a .nvmrc file in the current directory, set the local nvmrc_node_version to the Node version specified in .nvmrcIf the required version is not installed, then use nvm to install itIf it is installed then use nvm use to run that specific versionIf there is no .nvmrc file in the current directory then use the default installed Node versionAdd the load-nvmrc function to the chpwd hookRun the function to initialize it{.custom-ordered}The script looks like this:load-nvmrc() {\n' +
    '  # 1\n' +
    '  local node_version="$(nvm version)"\n' +
    '  local nvmrc_path="$(nvm_find_nvmrc)"\n' +
    '\n' +
    '  # 2\n' +
    '  if [ -n "$nvmrc_path" ]; then\n' +
    '    local nvmrc_node_version=$(nvm version "$(cat "${nvmrc_path}")")\n' +
    '\n' +
    '    # 3\n' +
    '    if [ "$nvmrc_node_version" = "N/A" ]; then\n' +
    '      nvm install\n' +
    '    # 4\n' +
    '    elif [ "$nvmrc_node_version" != "$node_version" ]; then\n' +
    '      nvm use\n' +
    '    fi\n' +
    '  # 5\n' +
    '  elif [ "$node_version" != "$(nvm version default)" ]; then\n' +
    '    echo "Reverting to nvm default version"\n' +
    '    nvm use default\n' +
    '  fi\n' +
    '}\n' +
    '\n' +
    '# 6\n' +
    'add-zsh-hook chpwd load-nvmrc\n' +
    '# 7\n' +
    'load-nvmrcIf we put this script in the account’s .zshrc file, the script will be available',
  readingTime: { text: '3 min read', minutes: 2.025, time: 121500, words: 405 }
}
