reading-time plugin: {
  textOnPage: 'Thanks to Kevin Powell and his video for showing me how to do a trick that has always intrigued me.<lite-youtube videoid="ypstT5UfCsk"></lite-youtube>The idea is that we have a border color that fades to transparent or invisible.This will take two items:The border image propertyThe linear gradient functionSetupthe HTML we will use looks like this<div class="container">\n' +
    '  <div class="row">\n' +
    '    <div class="item">\n' +
    '      <h2>Item Title</h2>\n' +
    '\n' +
    '      <p>item content</p>\n' +
    '    </div>\n' +
    '    <div class="item">\n' +
    '      <h2>Item Title</h2>\n' +
    '\n' +
    '      <p>Item content</p>\n' +
    '    </div>\n' +
    '    <div class="item">\n' +
    '      <h2>Item Title</h2>\n' +
    '\n' +
    '      <p>item content</p>\n' +
    '    </div>\n' +
    '  </div>We will also add some CSS to make make the row-based flex layout:.row {\n' +
    '  display: flex;\n' +
    '  gap: 2em;\n' +
    '  justify-content: space-evenly;\n' +
    '  padding: 2em;\n' +
    '}Creating the effectWith all the setup we did, creating the effect is fairly straightforward.We want the top and left border to start with a solid color and become invisible before the end of the border. The code does the following:Defines the borders we want to work with using logical propertiesIn English and other Western languages, block-start is top and inline-start is rightUse the border image property to set the image to a linear gradientgradients can be used everywhere an image canUse the border-image-slice method to make sure the image will appear in full. Otherwise, the image will only appear in the corners.item {\n' +
    '  /* 1 */\n' +
    '  padding: 1em;\n' +
    '  border-block-start: 5px solid;\n' +
    '  border-inline-start: 5px solid;\n' +
    '\n' +
    '  /* 2 */\n' +
    '  border-image-source: linear-gradient(45deg, rebeccapurple, transparent 75%);\n' +
    '  /* 3 */\n' +
    '  border-image-slice: 1;\n' +
    '}The code produces the following result:<iframe height="531.346435546875" style="width: 100%;" scrolling="no" title="gradients in background-image" src="https://codepen.io/caraya/embed/LYmqZqQ?default-tab=result" frameborder="no" loading="lazy" allowtransparency="true" allowfullscreen="true">See the Pen <a href="https://codepen.io/caraya/pen/LYmqZqQ"> gradients in background-image</a> by Carlos Araya (<a href="https://codepen.io/caraya">@caraya</a>) on <a href="https://codepen.io">CodePen</a>. </iframe>',
  readingTime: { text: '2 min read', minutes: 1.295, time: 77700, words: 259 }
}
