reading-time plugin: {
  textOnPage: 'Radial gradients radiate out from a central point that you control.The first example is a gradient between two colors.The default position for the gradient is 50% 50%, at the center of the containing block.Because we didn’t specify dimensions for the color stops, the browser will use its default algorithm to create the gradient..demo01 {\n' +
    '  background:\n' +
    '    radial-gradient(\n' +
    '      red,\n' +
    '      blue\n' +
    '    );\n' +
    '}The second demo shows a three color gradient placed at the default location of 50% 50%..demo02 {\n' +
    '  background: \n' +
    '    radial-gradient(\n' +
    '      red,\n' +
    '      green,\n' +
    '      blue\n' +
    '    );\n' +
    '}There are two types of radial gradients: circular and elliptical. The default shape is circular.They will each produce a different result.demo03 produces a circular gradient and demo04 creates an ellyptical one..demo03 {\n' +
    '  background: \n' +
    '    radial-gradient(\n' +
    '      circle,\n' +
    '      red,\n' +
    '      blue\n' +
    '    );\n' +
    '}\n' +
    '\n' +
    '.demo04 {\n' +
    '  background: \n' +
    '    radial-gradient(\n' +
    '      ellipse,\n' +
    '      red,\n' +
    '      blue\n' +
    '    );\n' +
    '}Besides controlling the origin and the type of gradient, we can control the position of each color stop, either as percentages or fixed length values..demo05 {\n' +
    '  background:   \n' +
    '    radial-gradient(\n' +
    '      red,\n' +
    '      green 20%,\n' +
    '      blue 40%,\n' +
    '      cyan 20%,\n' +
    '      hotpink\n' +
    '    );\n' +
    '}\n' +
    '\n' +
    '.demo06 {\n' +
    '  background: radial-gradient(\n' +
    '    red,\n' +
    '    green 200px,\n' +
    '    blue 100px,\n' +
    '    cyan 100px,\n' +
    '    hotpink\n' +
    '  );\n' +
    '}Unlike linear gradients, we can control the size of a radial gradient.It tales one of four possible values:closest-corner: sets the size as the distance from the starting point to the closest side of the enclosing boxclosest-side: sets the circle’s radius to be the distance between the center of the gradient and the closest sidefarthest-corner (default): sets the size of the gradient by the distance from the starting point to the farthest corner of the enclosing boxfarthest-side: sets the size of the gradient by the distance from the starting point to the farthest side..demo07 {\n' +
    '  background-image:\n' +
    '    radial-gradient(\n' +
    '      farthest-corner at 40px 40px,\n' +
    '      #f35 0%,\n' +
    '      #43e 100%\n' +
    '    );\n' +
    '}\n' +
    '\n' +
    '.demo08 {\n' +
    '  background-image: radial-gradient(\n' +
    '    closest-corner at 40px 40px,\n' +
    '    #f35 0%,\n' +
    '    #43e 100%\n' +
    '  );\n' +
    '}\n' +
    '\n' +
    '.demo09 {\n' +
    '  background-image: radial-gradient(\n' +
    '    closest-side at 40px 40px,\n' +
    '    #f35 0%,\n' +
    '    #43e 100%\n' +
    '  );\n' +
    '}\n' +
    '\n' +
    '.demo10 {\n' +
    '  background-image: radial-gradient(\n' +
    '    farthest-side at 40px 40px,\n' +
    '    #f35 0%,\n' +
    '    #43e 100%\n' +
    '  );\n' +
    '}We can also combine the gradient shape, the gradient size and the gradient size in a single statement.demo11 shows the combined statements for a circle-shaped gradient while demo12 shows the combined statements for an ellipsis gradient..demo11 {\n' +
    '  background-image: radial-gradient(\n' +
    '    circle farthest-side at 0 50%,\n' +
    '    hotpink,\n' +
    '    blueviolet 20%,\n' +
    '    blue 30%,\n' +
    '    lightblue\n' +
    '  );\n' +
    '}\n' +
    '\n' +
    '.demo12 {\n' +
    '  background-image: radial-gradient(\n' +
    '    ellipse farthest-side at 0 50%,\n' +
    '    red,\n' +
    '    yellow 10%,\n' +
    '    #1e90ff 50%,\n' +
    '    beige\n' +
    '  );\n' +
    '}The final example shows stacked radial gradients.demo13 {\n' +
    '  background: radial-gradient(\n' +
    '    circle at 50% 0,\n' +
    '    rgba(255, 0, 0, 0.5),\n' +
    '    rgba(255, 0, 0, 0) 70.71%\n' +
    '  ),\n' +
    '  radial-gradient(\n' +
    '    circle at 6.7% 75%,\n' +
    '    rgba(0, 0, 255, 0.5),\n' +
    '    rgba(0, 0, 255, 0) 70.71%\n' +
    '  ),\n' +
    '  radial-gradient(\n' +
    '    circle at 93.3% 75%,\n' +
    '    rgba(0, 255, 0, 0.5),\n' +
    '    rgba(0, 255, 0, 0) 70.71%\n' +
    '  )\n' +
    '  beige;\n' +
    '  border-radius: 50%;\n' +
    '}',
  readingTime: { text: '3 min read', minutes: 2.265, time: 135900, words: 453 }
}
